.TH LAUNCHER-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-16" "launcher-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
launcher-revamped \- terminal apps one key away in tmux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B launcher-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.br
.B launcher-revamped
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B list
.br
.B launcher-revamped launch
.I id
.RI [ arg ...]
.br
.B launcher-revamped pick
.br
.B launcher-revamped launch\-picked
.br
.B launcher-revamped doctor
.br
.B launcher-revamped version
.br
.B launcher-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B launcher-revamped
opens the terminal apps you list, such as lazygit, yazi or htop, in a tmux
popup, window or split that starts in the current pane's folder. A menu on
.B prefix M\-a
lists every app, and any app can have a key of its own. The entry point
.B launcher-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, and every binding goes to tmux in one call.
A menu key the person bound before the plugin loaded stays theirs.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind every key now.
.TP
.B list
Print every binding apply would make, one per line.
.TP
.BI launch " id"
Open the app
.IR id .
Each word after it is appended to the app's command as one quoted argument.
.TP
.B pick
Choose an app with
.BR fzf (1)
and record it in the tmux option
.BR @launcher_revamped_picked .
.TP
.B launch\-picked
Open the app pick recorded, and clear it.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the core tools, fzf for the picker, each
app's command, a menu key the person had already bound, and gum. The app rows
appear only when no core tool is missing. Exits 1 only when a required tool
is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-menu\-key
or
.BR \-\-lazygit\-key .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LAUNCHER_REVAMPED_SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR LAUNCHER_REVAMPED_LAZYGIT_KEY .
The command line wins over the environment, and the environment over the
tmux option. An empty value leaves that key unbound.
.TP
.B LAUNCHER_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B LAUNCHER_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B LAUNCHER_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B LAUNCHER_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.TP
.B LAUNCHER_PATH
Set for an app's
.B _if
check: the folder the app would start in.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default.
.TP
.B @launcher_revamped_apps
The app IDs the menu lists and the keys come from. The default is
.BR "lazygit yazi" .
.TP
.B @launcher_revamped_menu_key
The prefix key for the menu of every app. The default is
.BR M\-a ;
.B none
binds no menu.
.TP
.B @launcher_revamped_picker_key
The prefix key for the fzf app picker. Unbound until set.
.TP
.B @launcher_revamped_marker
A file or folder, such as
.BR .git ,
that every app without its own marker looks for: the app starts in the
nearest folder above the pane's that holds it.
.TP
.B @launcher_revamped_max_depth
How many folders the marker search climbs. The default is
.BR 20 .
.TP
.B @launcher_revamped_skip_missing
.B on
binds no key for an app whose command is not installed; an app with a host
is not checked. The default is
.BR off .
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _key
The app's own prefix key. Unbound until set.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _command
What the app runs. The default is the ID.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _mode
.BR popup ,
.B window
or
.BR split .
The default is
.BR popup ,
and
.B window
for yazi. A popup needs tmux 3.2; an older tmux opens a window.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _name
The window name and the menu label. The default is the ID.
.TP
.BR @launcher_revamped_ \fIid\fR _width ", " @launcher_revamped_ \fIid\fR _height
The popup size. The default is
.BR 80% .
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _marker
The app's own project marker.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _if
A shell check run first; a non-zero exit keeps the app closed.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _prompt
A prompt shown before the launch; each typed word becomes a quoted argument.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _group
App IDs opened in one new window, tiled.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _host
A host the app runs on, through
.BR "ssh \-t" .
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _reuse
.B on
selects the app's window when one with its name is open, in window mode.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _env
Variables set before the command with
.BR env ,
such as
.BR A=1 .
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _pre
A command that must succeed before the app starts.
.TP
.BI @launcher_revamped_ id _exit
A command run after the app exits.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR gum (1)
